        "parms": "# sustain — a sustain pedal\nsustain holds note releases back while its pedal is down, as a piano's sustain pedal does. A pitch on the left inlet goes out with the velocity stored on the middle inlet. A note-on always passes. A release, velocity 0, passes with the pedal up and is held with the pedal down. The right inlet is the pedal: a number other than 0 presses it, and 0 lifts it and sends every held release, lowest pitch first. The messages sustain 1 and sustain 0 do the same on the left inlet.\nMax's sustain has a repeatmode attribute for a key played again while its release is held. Here the key sounds again and its held release still goes out when the pedal lifts, Max's default.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
